# Class / series availability handling

## Goal

> **Puddles helps parents understand fit and enrollment; the provider is the source of truth for real-time availability.**

## Do not show on public listings

- Exact open seats by day/time (“Open seats as of Aug 27: Mon 9:30…”)
- Section-by-section waitlist status (“Waitlist: Fri 9:30 & 10:30”)
- Dated availability snapshots that will go stale within days
- **Open** or **Available** badges unless status can be refreshed reliably (automated feed or same-day manual refresh)

## Keep on Puddles (stable)

- Series date range (e.g. Sep 9–Nov 18)
- Recurring days pattern (e.g. Mon, Wed & Fri options)
- Age fit
- Registration required vs drop-in
- Semester/package vs single session
- Free demo or trial availability (when offered as a standing policy)
- Venue and what the experience is for little ones

## For changing availability

Use general language and link out:

> Some sections may fill or move to waitlist — check the official registration page for current availability.

Link `eventUrl` to the provider’s official registration or schedule page. Do not duplicate “Register at …” in tips when the official link button already goes there.

## Internal vs public

- `lastChecked` / verified date → admin only; not shown to parents on cards or detail
- Seat-level notes may live in **calendar watchlist** or discovery admin notes for editors — not in `description` or `tips` on live events

## Series rows

Semester and multi-section programs = **one series row**, not weekly Browse spam. See `parent-and-me-events.mdc`.

## Examples

| Avoid | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| Open seats as of Aug 27: Mon 9:30, Wed 10:30 | Multiple Mon, Wed & Fri class times available |
| Fri 9:30 waitlist | Some sections may fill or move to waitlist — check the official registration page |
| Several currently open for registration | Registration required · semester package, not drop-in |

